+# Specification Quality Checklist: Pastebin Service
+
+**Purpose**: Validate specification completeness and quality before proceeding to planning
+**Created**: 2026-11-09
+**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md)
+
+## Content Quality
+
+- [x] No implementation details (languages, frameworks, APIs) — *with a documented exception, see Notes 1*
+- [x] Focused on user value and business needs
+- [x] Written for non-technical stakeholders
+- [x] All mandatory sections completed
+
+## Requirement Completeness
+
+- [x] No [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers remain
+- [x] Requirements are testable and unambiguous
+- [x] Success criteria are measurable
+- [x] Success criteria are technology-agnostic (no implementation details)
+- [x] All acceptance scenarios are defined
+- [x] Edge cases are identified
+- [x] Scope is clearly bounded
+- [x] Dependencies and assumptions identified
+
+## Feature Readiness
+
+- [x] All functional requirements have clear acceptance criteria
+- [x] User scenarios cover primary flows
+- [x] Feature meets measurable outcomes defined in Success Criteria
+- [x] No implementation details leak into specification — *see Notes 1*
+
+## Notes
+
+1. **Documented exception — the API contract is the product.** The feature request specified
+   the exact endpoint paths, HTTP methods, header name (`X-Delete-Token`), JSON field names,
+   status codes, and the runtime platform (Python 3.11+, standard library only, a `pastebin`
+   package under `src/`). For a service whose entire user interface *is* its HTTP API, these
+   are the observable behaviour, not implementation choices, so they belong in the
+   requirements. Two containment measures were applied so the exception stays bounded:
+   - Requirements FR-001–FR-037 are written in behavioural terms ("report not found",
+     "acknowledge with a no-content success response") with the mandated status code given
+     in parentheses, rather than as instructions about code.
+   - Platform and packaging constraints — Python version, dependency ban, `src/pastebin`
+     layout, command form — are quarantined in a separate **Constraints** section marked as
+     imposed by the request, and are deliberately absent from the Functional Requirements and
+     Success Criteria.
+
+   Success criteria SC-001–SC-008 are free of technology references and verifiable without
+   knowing how the service is built.
+
+2. **Deliberate under-specification, recorded in Assumptions rather than as clarifications.**
+   Four details were left open because no reasonable default is load-bearing and each is
+   genuinely an implementation choice: identifier and credential length/alphabet, the
+   on-disk layout within the storage directory, whether expired snippets are reclaimed
+   eagerly or lazily, and behaviour under a backwards clock jump. Each is named explicitly in
+   the Assumptions section so that planning knows it is free to decide.
+
+3. **Constitution alignment.** The standard-library-only constraint matches Principle I. The
+   error requirements (FR-005, FR-006, FR-032–FR-037) encode Principle II: every specified
+   failure mode has a named, explanatory outcome and none may be swallowed. SC-008 encodes
+   Principle III by requiring each FR identifier to be named by at least one passing test.
+
+4. Items marked incomplete require spec updates before `/speckit-clarify` or `/speckit-plan`.
+   None are incomplete.
